  "details": "This one is a bit odd-ish, but if you try to build anything at all - you'll hit it. I was trying to make an area trigger that toggles object and in the process I tried to log the intermediate values, upon which the connections would break, rendering the whole thing not working.\nSame sometimes happens if you insert a node into a current flow path, like adding a log before some action.\n\nSee attached gifs for examples\n\nSometimes you would also only see the connections break on entering/exiting the playmode\n\nThe whole situation made making of a simple graph a game of cat and mouse tracking the connections that broke until the breaking went away and the program finally worked. Also attached the error that i saw in my log, but i do not know if it popped up exactly when the connections broke\n\n> As a sidenote - if I would copy paste those graphs (with lines, supposedly connected) into a current live - the lines would be missing where they would break in the beta\n\nIssue is only present in the Open Beta SDK released with the build 1080 (sdk 2021.04.16.12.12). It is good on current Live (sdk 2021.03.22.18.27)",
